"onboarding.accountBalanceGuideCash" = "This one's the most straightforward: how much cash do you have right now? Check your wallet, that drawer, or wherever you keep your physical money.\n\nDon't worry about being exact — if you think you have \"around 50\", go with 50. You can always adjust it later.";
"onboarding.accountBalanceGuideChecking" = "Your checking (or debit) account has an available balance you can look up in your banking app or at an ATM.\n\nEnter the available balance you see today. If you have several checking accounts, you can create one account in Yala for each, or group them together — whatever works for you.";
"onboarding.accountBalanceGuideClosing" = "Don't worry if it's not perfect — the important thing is to get started.";
"onboarding.accountBalanceGuideGeneral" = "If you're using a general account to group all your payment methods in one currency, your balance reflects how much money you have available.\n\nTo calculate it, add up everything: checking accounts, savings, cash. If you have pending credit card charges, you can subtract them for a more precise picture — or track each card as a separate account later.\n\nThat final number is your initial balance.";
"onboarding.accountBalanceGuideIntro" = "Your initial balance tells Yala how much money you're starting with. It doesn't need to be exact to the penny — a rough estimate works great. Here's how to think about it depending on the type of account you chose.";
"onboarding.accountBalanceGuideSavings" = "How much do you have saved up in your savings accounts? If you have several, you can create one account in Yala for each or combine them into one.\n\nEnter the total you have saved. If your bank shows accrued interest, include it in the total.";
"onboarding.accountBalanceGuideTitle" = "How do I calculate my balance?";
